## What you'll leave with

- **Four diagrams on a whiteboard**, photographed before anyone erases anything. A photo of a whiteboard is a legitimate diagram for your draft; polish is not the point today.
- **Two decisions argued in writing**, which is section 6 of your design document already drafted.
- **A section of the draft assigned to each person** on your team, named out loud before you leave the room.
- **The hard 80% of the design document**, which is why the draft is due the next day rather than the next week. The boards are the work; the evening is transcription.

